WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.513
Three operators that may be less familiar are
exponent floor division and modulo Exponent

00:00:06.526 --> 00:00:12.355
raises a value to a power Floor division gives the
whole-number quotient and modulo

00:00:12.382 --> 00:00:18.699
gives the remainder A practical example is time
conversion If

00:00:18.725 --> 00:00:23.028
we have one hundred eighty five minutes floor
division by sixty tells us the number

00:00:23.054 --> 00:00:29.752
of complete hours Modulo sixty tells us the minutes
that remain Run

00:00:29.778 --> 00:00:35.163
the example on the slide then try the one hundred
eighty five minute example These

00:00:35.189 --> 00:00:40.886
operators also appear in bucketing periodic rules
indexing patterns and many other programming

00:00:40.913 --> 00:00:41.465
tasks
